// Compiler options for the tests, used by ts-jest. Identical to the build's, except that the tests
// get jest's globals.
//
// Keeping "types" out of tsconfig.json is what makes a test-only identifier left behind in shipped
// source a compile error rather than something that builds cleanly.
//
// src/**/*.d.ts is load-bearing rather than tidiness: the ambient "*.scss" and "*.svg" declarations
// live there, the components under test import those files, and ambient declarations are reached by
// being included, never by being imported.
//
// "exclude" is deliberately not set. The base config does not define one, so it inherits TypeScript's
// default, which keeps node_modules out. Resetting it to [] here would pull node_modules in.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "types": ["jest"]
  },
  "include": ["./src/**/*.test.ts", "./src/**/*.test.tsx", "./src/**/*.d.ts"]
}
